<p>
  The sheet is a <code>Y.Array</code> named <code>rows</code>. Each row is a
  <code>Y.Map</code> keyed by column, and each cell in it is another
  <code>Y.Map</code> holding <code>value</code>, <code>bold</code>, and
  <code>fill</code>. Since those are separate keys, one person can bold a cell
  while someone else types in it and both changes survive. Two writes to the
  same key resolve as last write wins. A value is saved when you press Enter
  or leave the cell, as in most spreadsheets.
</p>
<p>
  TanStack Table handles sorting and column order separately in each window,
  and neither is written to the shared document. Sort by Owner in one window
  and by Qty in the other, then edit the same row in both.
</p>
